ists who  like to draw angels take note  this is how you should be drawing your  angels anatomy  if you don't like this if it looks too  weird for you  this will  let's give her some music so she's not  shuffling around in silence  there we go  this woman does seem to have figured out  a reasonable alternative  just having the feathers come right off  the arms that is literally how birds do  it  my name is john perry  angel wings are fake  merry christmas  if you enjoyed today's science lesson  you should definitely subscribe to this  channel do that right now but also you  are invited to come hang out with me in  ecuador where my friend nancy and i are  planning an evolution tour of the amazon  jungle nancy is an entomologist a  scientist who studies bugs and she lives  in ecuador it will be a week-long tour  of the mountain range the cloud forest  and the amazon jungle we will hike  through the forests paddle around on  boats and in the evenings nancy and i  will give lessons on evolution kind of  like the one that you just watched here  but you know relevant to jungle stuff  you are guaranteed to see all sorts of  amazing wildlife that you've never seen  before  if lucky we might even see river  dolphins which i'm really excited about  i've never seen a river dolphin before  exact details are not available yet but  we do have a website where you can sign  up for our mailing list and see a bunch  of photos from past tours link to the  website is down in the video description  we're thinking it will be the week of  new year's day  2023 i know that's a ways out there i  suppose we could do it sooner but i want  the world to have a bit of a better  handle on covid before i invite a bunch  of people to travel across international  borders nancy is working with hotels and  a tour bus company so that everything  food lodging salaries and tips for the  local tour guides and all of your travel  within ecuador for eight days will be  less than two thousand per person  exac